      "content": "thanks for this. it's a decent start, but it's a bit thin on the actual technical details per section. \n\ni just ran it through our automated comprehensiveness checker and the score was pretty low (it's coming back around 15-20). i know i said not to game it, but for the CI/CD pipeline to even flag this for human review, we really need that score to be higher. \n\ncan you expand on the \"Setting Up Your Environment\" and \"Working with Data Streams\" sections? try to add more granular steps and specifics for the devs. just... keep it readable, please. i don't want a wall of single-sentence bullets, but we definitely need more structural elements to satisfy the checker.",
