      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "# Getting Started with CloudScale DataStream API\n\nThis guide walks you through setting up and working with CloudScale DataStream API to harness the power of real-time data streaming.\n\n## Prerequisites\nBefore beginning, you should have:\n\n- A CloudScale workspace.\n- Necessary permissions set.\n- An understanding of REST API principles.\n\n### Setting Up Your Environment\n\n#### Authentication\n1. **Access Credentials**\n   Access a set of unique user IDs and cryptographic keys, ensuring that only you can tap into their unique data set.\n2. **API Tokens**\n   Generate a bearer token using OAuth 2.0 for authenticating API requests.\n\n#### Data Stream Configuration\n1. **Data Stream Declaration**\n   - Describe your data stream by specifying its name, source, and intended transformations or computations.\n2. **Parameter Tuning**\n   - Tailor your stream's parameters, from sample rate to window size, to match its expected load and latency requirements.\n3. **Stream Preview**\n   - Use the simulation tool to visualize the flow of data into and out of the stream to ensure correctness before going live.\n\n#### Deployment Strategy\n1. **Resource Allocation**\n   - Provision computational resources efficiently to manage stream data throughput effectively.\n2. **Monitoring",
      "source": "target",
